    <!-- Advice under the score: at most one line, and only when the numbers prove it -->
    <string name="advice_sound_check">Most of your strokes did not land near a note. That is the sound, not your playing \u2014 run the sound check.</string>
    <string name="advice_sound_check_action">Sound check</string>
    <string name="advice_detector">%1$d%% of your strokes were too quiet to count. Play a little harder, or move the phone closer to the pad.</string>
    <string name="advice_extras">More strokes than notes: %1$d%% extra. A rebounding stick or a noisy room \u2014 both are heard as strokes.</string>
    <string name="advice_offset_late">You play %1$d ms behind the click, every stroke. Aim to hit with the click, not after it.</string>
    <string name="advice_offset_early">You play %1$d ms ahead of the click, every stroke. Let the click arrive before the stick.</string>
    <string name="advice_offset_gain">Your evenness alone is worth %1$d%%: that is what this level scores once the lateness is gone.</string>
    <string name="advice_drift_faster">You speed up: by the end you are %1$d ms ahead of where you started.</string>
    <string name="advice_drift_slower">You slow down: by the end you are %1$d ms behind where you started.</string>
    <string name="advice_spread">Your strokes wander by \u00b1%1$d ms. Drop the tempo until they stop wandering, then bring it back.</string>
    <string name="advice_all_good">Even, and nothing to fix at this tempo. Take the next one.</string>
